/**
 * The outcome status as **stated by the backend** (STORY-98 / ISSUE-140).
 *
 * The SDK does not decide this. Before this existed, the SDK's model of PG's reply carried only a
 * response code, so six separate places each invented a status by pattern-matching that code — and
 * they disagreed: the same `96` was a decline in the EMV kernel and a failure in wallet history.
 * The failure direction was always the same, and always the costly one: an outcome PG had recorded
 * as *unresolved* was reported to the merchant as a decline, with no store and no poll, on a
 * payment the customer may have been charged for.
 *
 * Only [APPROVED], [DECLINED] and [FAILED] are final. [PENDING] always means "ask again".
 *
 * [Unknown] exists because SDKs live on merchant devices for months while the backend ships weekly:
 * a status added after this build must degrade, never crash and never be coerced into a neighbour
 * (`devices/CLAUDE.md` §15). An unknown status is **not** an outcome — treat it as unresolved.
 *
 * @note annotations
 *   kotlinx.serialization.Serializable
*/
