/**
 * Token lifecycle status from the server.
 * Only ACTIVE tokens can perform transactions (GPO, Read Record, Generate AC).
 *
 * Hoisted from androidMain to commonMain (STORY-66) so the shared lifecycle sync and the
 * cross-platform pay flows gate on the same vocabulary.
 *
 * Public since STORY-99 (ISSUE-84 item 5): Android's `tokenStatus` read and `Token.status`
 * return it, so a host can say "suspended — call your bank" vs "pending — enter your code" vs
 * "expired — re-add the card" instead of one grey card.
 *
 * **One parse, and an unknown status is not payable** (ISSUE-170 step 2, instructor ruling
 * 2026-08-10). This enum used to carry two parses: `fromWire` for public reads (unknown →
 * [UNKNOWN], "never a neighbour") and `fromString` for the gates and storage (unknown/blank →
 * [ACTIVE], "for backward compatibility"). The second was the fail-open the issue is about — the
 * gate manufactured a payable status out of a value it did not understand, which is how a
 * freshly digitised card came to pay: digitise wrote `APPROVED` into this field, no member
 * matched, and the default made it ACTIVE. With digitise now writing lifecycle values
 * ([co.veyra.wallet.sdk.api.DigitiseResponseCode]) and legacy rows normalised on read, nothing
 * depends on that fallthrough any more, so there is one [parse] and unknown means [UNKNOWN].
 *
 * The consequence is deliberate: a card whose stored status this build cannot classify **does not
 * pay** until a status sync says otherwise. That refuses in the recoverable direction — a poll
 * restores payability within seconds — where the old default paid on a guess.
 */
