/**
 * Seam (STORY-33 Phase 2): device-integrity **attestation**.
 *
 * The wallet's digitise/provision flow asks for a platform attestation token bound to a server
 * nonce; the **backend** validates it and decides whether to digitise. This is one of the three
 * irreducibly platform-specific wallet seams (with [DeviceKeyStore] and [SecureStorage]) — there is
 * no shared logic to extract, only two separate platform implementations behind this contract:
 *
 * - **androidMain actual:** hardware Key Attestation ([KeyAttestor] — STORY-71; an attested
 *   throwaway Keystore key's certificate chain, no Google credentials on either side).
 * - **iosMain actual:** App Attest (`AppAttestDeviceAttestor` → `DCAppAttestService`); needs the
 *   App Attest capability + a real device (unsupported on the simulator).
 *
 * **`attest` never fails the caller (STORY-36 slice 5).** Producing an attestation blob is a device
 * *capability* — the simulator, an old/rooted device, a missing entitlement, or a transient platform
 * error can all prevent it. Whether an unattested (or attested-but-invalid) request may still
 * digitise is the **server's** policy call, not the client's, so the attestor returns an
 * [AttestationResult] describing what it could produce (with a [status] reason when it couldn't)
 * rather than throwing; the flow always sends the request and lets the backend rule.
 */
